('advanced-native-2073', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2073-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["She made the correction available for checking and explained what had gone wrong."],"options":["She asked people to trust her title without seeing the corrected record.","She withheld the changed list until everyone had promised to accept her account.","The account confirms that every person now trusts her and will not question another decision.","She made the correction available for checking and explained what had gone wrong."]},"advanced-native-2073-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The error was acknowledged in a way others could examine for themselves.","She gave the correction and its reason, while leaving people able to check them.","She tried to earn people’s trust through an explanation and a corrected list they could check.","She let people inspect the change instead of relying only on her assurance."],"options":["The error was acknowledged in a way others could examine for themselves.","She gave the correction and its reason, while leaving people able to check them.","She tried to earn people’s trust through an explanation and a corrected list they could check.","She let people inspect the change instead of relying only on her assurance."]},"advanced-native-2073-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The title and request alone do not show that he has earned people’s trust through reliable conduct."],"options":["The title and request alone do not show that he has earned people’s trust through reliable conduct.","The introduction describes a completed correction that members could inspect.","The account reports members’ confidence based on a sustained record of keeping commitments."]},"advanced-native-2073-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Everyone has already agreed to trust her without further questions."],"options":["She wants to gain others’ confidence through how she acts.","Everyone has already agreed to trust her without further questions.","More context could describe the commitments and actions involved."]},"advanced-native-2073-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["She can earn people’s trust by making the correction checkable; allowing questions supports that process rather than cancelling it."],"options":["I would remove access to the list after the explanation, so people could show confidence by not checking.","I would count the explanation itself as confirmation that every person now agrees with her next decision.","She can earn people’s trust by making the correction checkable; allowing questions supports that process rather than cancelling it."]},"advanced-native-2073-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I hope to earn people’s trust by keeping a record of decisions and reasons that members can read, and by asking before using anyone’s story. Please send me questions through this group or speak with me after the meeting; the title alone is not a reason to stop asking.","Being chosen does not automatically earn people’s trust, so I want to make my commitments clear: readable decision notes and permission before sharing personal accounts. You can ask me here or after a meeting, and I will explain what I can and what still needs checking."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2074', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2074-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Friday is the current return plan, while the person collecting the screens is still being checked."],"options":["The collecting person has been confirmed, while there is no proposed return day.","The organiser has promised the plan cannot change if new information arrives.","Friday is the current return plan, while the person collecting the screens is still being checked.","The screens have already been returned and the message only records the completed handover."]},"advanced-native-2074-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The current plan is Friday, with one practical detail still being checked.","We have a proposed day, not a record that the screens are already back.","The organiser can report the present plan while making clear that collection has not been fully arranged.","As things stand now, Friday is possible, but the collecting person still needs confirmation."],"options":["The current plan is Friday, with one practical detail still being checked.","We have a proposed day, not a record that the screens are already back.","The organiser can report the present plan while making clear that collection has not been fully arranged.","As things stand now, Friday is possible, but the collecting person still needs confirmation."]},"advanced-native-2074-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A statement about how things stood on Monday does not replace the confirmed Wednesday update; we should report the current position."],"options":["The Monday qualifier makes the earlier repair status permanent despite the later confirmed reopening.","The Wednesday notice is described as an unconfirmed hope, rather than a confirmed reopening.","A statement about how things stood on Monday does not replace the confirmed Wednesday update; we should report the current position."]},"advanced-native-2074-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The start has already happened and no later information can affect it."],"options":["The start has already happened and no later information can affect it.","A later update may revise the plan if the situation changes.","Next week is the plan given the present situation."]},"advanced-native-2074-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["As things stand now, Friday is the plan; we can say that and clearly identify the collection detail still being checked."],"options":["As things stand now, Friday is the plan; we can say that and clearly identify the collection detail still being checked.","I would withhold the proposed day until every detail is fixed, even though people need the current plan to arrange their time.","I would announce Friday as a completed handover so nobody needs to ask about collection."]},"advanced-native-2074-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["As things stand now, we know where the note was found, not who put it there. I would compare the sequence and the characters’ movements in the next chapter before our notes identify a character as the person who left it.","As things stand now, the empty room is part of the evidence, but it does not identify who left the note there. Let us keep the conclusion open while we check the timing and what each character could actually have done."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2075', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2075-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["She gained new knowledge, questioned an earlier interpretation of quietness and practised different ways to check understanding."],"options":["The new class had already been assessed using one unchanged method, and no further learning was described.","She gained new knowledge, questioned an earlier interpretation of quietness and practised different ways to check understanding.","She repeated the old assumption more quickly without examining how the new pupils communicated.","She discarded every teaching skill she had and stopped checking pupils’ understanding."]},"advanced-native-2075-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She had to learn, unlearn, and relearn, including revising what she thought a quiet response meant.","She learned about the pupils’ languages and stopped assuming that quietness always signalled confusion.","New information changed an earlier interpretation and led to different checking practices.","She kept developing her teaching by asking different questions rather than simply repeating the same assumption."],"options":["She had to learn, unlearn, and relearn, including revising what she thought a quiet response meant.","She learned about the pupils’ languages and stopped assuming that quietness always signalled confusion.","New information changed an earlier interpretation and led to different checking practices.","She kept developing her teaching by asking different questions rather than simply repeating the same assumption."]},"advanced-native-2075-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Faster repetition alone does not show someone working through a cycle of “learn, unlearn, and relearn”; the account gives no revised assumption or approach."],"options":["The account identifies a new rule that replaced the earlier folding method.","The volunteer has stopped using the confirmed list because new evidence showed it was outdated.","Faster repetition alone does not show someone working through a cycle of “learn, unlearn, and relearn”; the account gives no revised assumption or approach."]},"advanced-native-2075-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Every earlier skill must be erased before anything new can be learned."],"options":["The context should show what is being questioned and practised differently.","New learning can include revising an earlier assumption or habit.","Every earlier skill must be erased before anything new can be learned."]},"advanced-native-2075-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["She can learn, unlearn, and relearn while keeping useful experience; the change concerns an assumption about quiet pupils, not the loss of all teaching knowledge."],"options":["She can learn, unlearn, and relearn while keeping useful experience; the change concerns an assumption about quiet pupils, not the loss of all teaching knowledge.","I would describe the new class as proof that none of her earlier experience can be useful.","I would keep the earlier interpretation of quietness unchanged and focus only on making the same explanation louder."]},"advanced-native-2075-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I have had to learn, unlearn, and relearn while tracing this object: the letter shows it was a gift, not something its owner necessarily made. I will separate ownership from authorship in the label and check the evidence for each, rather than discard every earlier record.","Today I saw why I need to learn, unlearn, and relearn: I had treated an owner’s name as the maker’s, until the gift letter challenged that assumption. My next label will distinguish the two roles and state what is still unknown."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2076', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2076-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["She demonstrated, allowed practice and asked about remaining difficulties."],"options":["She demonstrated, allowed practice and asked about remaining difficulties.","She announced only the date and left users to discover the procedure alone.","She treated the lack of questions as proof that no demonstration was needed.","She completed every return for users without letting them try the new steps."]},"advanced-native-2076-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The support went beyond announcing when the new process began.","She tried to guide people through change with a demonstration, practice and a chance to explain difficulties.","Users could try a return and say which part they still needed help with.","She made the steps visible and checked what people had understood."],"options":["The support went beyond announcing when the new process began.","She tried to guide people through change with a demonstration, practice and a chance to explain difficulties.","Users could try a return and say which part they still needed help with.","She made the steps visible and checked what people had understood."]},"advanced-native-2076-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["An effort to guide people through change can include practical support while questions or disagreement remain; those responses do not erase the demonstration and practice."],"options":["The remaining questions show that users were given only a start date, with no chance to try the process.","The demonstration confirms that the users have agreed with the change.","An effort to guide people through change can include practical support while questions or disagreement remain; those responses do not erase the demonstration and practice."]},"advanced-native-2076-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Every person has already agreed with the change and needs no further help."],"options":["More context should identify the transition and the support.","They intend to offer direction and support during a transition.","Every person has already agreed with the change and needs no further help."]},"advanced-native-2076-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["If we want to guide people through change, we should let them try the steps and ask what is unclear before they have to use the process alone."],"options":["If we want to guide people through change, we should let them try the steps and ask what is unclear before they have to use the process alone.","I would replace the trial with another date reminder, without checking whether people understand the steps.","I would wait until people miss a return before telling them how to ask for help."]},"advanced-native-2076-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["If we want to guide people through change rather than assume agreement, could we offer an optional trial before deciding the final arrangement? We should ask how it affects existing care commitments and treat participation as feedback, not permanent consent.","To guide people through change, I suggest a small voluntary trial followed by a discussion of its actual effects. Let us hear the care-related difficulties before choosing what to adopt, without treating a trial place as a promise to continue."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2078', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2078-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Practice and feedback make preparation more accessible, while a training application is still needed."],"options":["The account describes only a friendlier course title, with no change in support.","The guides had completed the next training programme before the practice visits were offered.","Practice and feedback make preparation more accessible, while a training application is still needed.","The mentoring has already replaced the application with a confirmed appointment."]},"advanced-native-2078-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The new mentoring gives novices a way to practise before applying.","They have more practical support for preparing, not an automatic place.","Feedback and visits reduce some of the difficulty of starting the route.","The path is becoming more open through practice visits and feedback, although a place still requires an application."],"options":["The new mentoring gives novices a way to practise before applying.","They have more practical support for preparing, not an automatic place.","Feedback and visits reduce some of the difficulty of starting the route.","The path is becoming more open through practice visits and feedback, although a place still requires an application."]},"advanced-native-2078-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A friendlier title alone does not establish that the path is becoming more open; the account still needs an actual access or support change."],"options":["The account describes new practice sessions and a different way to apply.","The course has already confirmed places for people unable to use its previous timetable.","A friendlier title alone does not establish that the path is becoming more open; the account still needs an actual access or support change."]},"advanced-native-2078-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Everyone has already reached the goal and no conditions remain."],"options":["Everyone has already reached the goal and no conditions remain.","More context should explain what change makes the route easier.","Access or feasibility is improving relative to an earlier situation."]},"advanced-native-2078-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The path is becoming more open because there is preparation support, but we should still explain the application and any conditions clearly."],"options":["I took the mentoring invitation to mean that my place on the next course was already confirmed.","I assumed the practice visits were the training itself, rather than preparation for a later application.","The path is becoming more open because there is preparation support, but we should still explain the application and any conditions clearly."]},"advanced-native-2078-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["With remote participation and equipment loans, the path is becoming more open for me, but I would like to check the arrangements before applying. Could you explain equipment booking, how the materials are sent and whether places remain?","The path is becoming more open now that travel is no longer the only way to take part. Before I submit an application, may I ask how to reserve equipment and receive the writing materials, and whether there is still space?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2079', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2079-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The story gives unequal extra demands after the same demonstration, without a relevant explanation."],"options":["The panel has removed the extra task, and the account only describes the replacement policy.","The story gives unequal extra demands after the same demonstration, without a relevant explanation.","The panel asks every applicant to complete the same extra task for a clearly stated role requirement.","The story says the women refused the shared demonstration before any comparison could be made."]},"advanced-native-2079-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It criticises expecting the women to prove themselves twice over after the same demonstration.","Only those applicants face another task without a relevant reason for treating them differently.","The shared demonstration is followed by a higher burden for one group.","The concern is the unequal requirement, not a stated finding that those applicants lack ability."],"options":["It criticises expecting the women to prove themselves twice over after the same demonstration.","Only those applicants face another task without a relevant reason for treating them differently.","The shared demonstration is followed by a higher burden for one group.","The concern is the unequal requirement, not a stated finding that those applicants lack ability."]},"advanced-native-2079-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Two shared, explained requirements alone do not establish that one group must prove themselves twice over under an unequal standard."],"options":["The account says only one group must submit the second piece without an explanation.","The panel has waived the requirements for some applicants while retaining both for the group in question.","Two shared, explained requirements alone do not establish that one group must prove themselves twice over under an unequal standard."]},"advanced-native-2079-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The speaker has established that the people concerned are less capable."],"options":["The context should show who is being asked for what and why the demand is criticised.","The speaker objects to an excessive or unequal demand for proof in context.","The speaker has established that the people concerned are less capable."]},"advanced-native-2079-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Being made to prove themselves twice over does not establish lower ability; we should describe the unequal requirement and ask what relevant reason the panel gives."],"options":["I assumed the extra task was for a different role, rather than an additional test for the same one.","Being made to prove themselves twice over does not establish lower ability; we should describe the unequal requirement and ask what relevant reason the panel gives.","I would use the extra task as a finding about ability, without comparing the actual demonstrations."]},"advanced-native-2079-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Applicants should not have to prove themselves twice over simply because they belong to that group. Could the proposal state the same role criteria for everyone and record a relevant reason whenever further evidence is needed?","Let us remove the automatic extra event rather than make one group prove themselves twice over. Any further evidence should follow the same stated criteria, with the reason explained, instead of being assigned by identity."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2080', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2080-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["There may be an improvement in access to senior roles, while other applicants’ experience still needs examining."],"options":["The narrator confirms that every barrier has disappeared from the whole institution.","The committee has kept all senior roles closed to the candidates it previously overlooked.","The changes concern entry-level roles only, while access to senior positions has remained the same.","There may be an improvement in access to senior roles, while other applicants’ experience still needs examining."]},"advanced-native-2080-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["There is a reason to investigate progress while keeping the remaining questions open.","The account recognises an opening without claiming that advancement is now equally easy for all.","The glass ceiling may be cracking, but the new process still needs to be examined across applicants.","Opening the senior roles gives a possible sign of change rather than a final conclusion about everyone."],"options":["There is a reason to investigate progress while keeping the remaining questions open.","The account recognises an opening without claiming that advancement is now equally easy for all.","The glass ceiling may be cracking, but the new process still needs to be examined across applicants.","Opening the senior roles gives a possible sign of change rather than a final conclusion about everyone."]},"advanced-native-2080-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The glass ceiling may be cracking in one respect, but this account does not establish that the remaining barriers have gone."],"options":["The account says those other candidates have now passed the previously blocking conditions.","The glass ceiling may be cracking in one respect, but this account does not establish that the remaining barriers have gone.","The appointment settles how the unexplained conditions affect every other candidate."]},"advanced-native-2080-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["All affected people now have the same opportunities and no barrier remains."],"options":["An invisible advancement barrier could be weakening.","All affected people now have the same opportunities and no barrier remains.","Further evidence can show the scope and limits of the possible change."]},"advanced-native-2080-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The glass ceiling may be cracking, and her appointment matters, but we still need to hear how the process treats other candidates."],"options":["The glass ceiling may be cracking, and her appointment matters, but we still need to hear how the process treats other candidates.","I took that one appointment to mean the unexplained conditions facing the other candidates had also been removed.","I assumed the appointment was only a proposal, because the narrator still asks questions about the wider process."]},"advanced-native-2080-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The glass ceiling may be cracking here, and I am delighted to congratulate you on what you have achieved. That does not make every extra mentoring request your responsibility; would you like help sorting the invitations before deciding which, if any, you want to accept?","The glass ceiling may be cracking, but your appointment should not turn into a duty to solve every remaining problem alone. Congratulations; if you would find it useful, I can help organise the requests so you can choose what fits your own time."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2081', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2081-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["A familiar response returned despite a changed system, and the speaker then checked the new index."],"options":["A familiar response returned despite a changed system, and the speaker then checked the new index.","The speaker had never used a catalogue before and was making a first guess.","The speaker deliberately chose the old system because the new index was unavailable.","The new order was identical to the familiar one, so no adjustment was needed."]},"advanced-native-2081-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["My first response came from long practice, but checking the updated index helped me adjust.","Old habits die hard; years of using that position made it my first response, even with the new index available.","The familiar order had become automatic, and I had to pause to use the new one.","I was repeating an established routine rather than deciding that the new index was wrong."],"options":["My first response came from long practice, but checking the updated index helped me adjust.","Old habits die hard; years of using that position made it my first response, even with the new index available.","The familiar order had become automatic, and I had to pause to use the new one.","I was repeating an established routine rather than deciding that the new index was wrong."]},"advanced-native-2081-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["One mistake alone does not establish the history behind saying old habits die hard; we still need to know whether an established routine is involved."],"options":["The report records the same placement being repeated over several years.","The newcomer says the old location became automatic through long practice.","One mistake alone does not establish the history behind saying old habits die hard; we still need to know whether an established routine is involved."]},"advanced-native-2081-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["No habit can ever change, so there is no reason to try a different approach."],"options":["An established routine can be difficult to change.","No habit can ever change, so there is no reason to try a different approach.","The context can describe a familiar response and an effort to interrupt it."]},"advanced-native-2081-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Old habits die hard, but that is a reason to pause and check the updated index, not a reason to ignore it."],"options":["I assumed my reaching for the old position meant the catalogue change was still only a proposal.","Old habits die hard, but that is a reason to pause and check the updated index, not a reason to ignore it.","I would leave the reminder until after I have searched the familiar position, rather than check the new index before starting."]},"advanced-native-2081-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Old habits die hard, but that does not excuse reaching for my phone while you were talking, and I am sorry. Next time I will put it in my bag before we begin; please tell me directly if I start drifting away again.","I am sorry my automatic phone-checking made it seem that I was not listening; old habits die hard, but I want to change this one. Could we begin with my phone in the bag, and could you point it out if I lose focus again?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2082', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2082-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["It asks how a focus on confident speeches leaves another kind of contribution unseen."],"options":["It says the organiser’s decisions were already given the same attention as the speeches.","It asks how a focus on confident speeches leaves another kind of contribution unseen.","It recommends choosing the organiser for quietness alone, without examining the decisions.","It treats the account as complete because the confident speeches are described in detail."]},"advanced-native-2082-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It questions the lens through which people view leadership when speeches eclipse the organiser’s decisions.","It asks why a visible speaking style receives attention while careful organising is overlooked.","The issue is which actions are treated as evidence of leadership.","It challenges a narrow account without claiming that one personality type always leads better."],"options":["It questions the lens through which people view leadership when speeches eclipse the organiser’s decisions.","It asks why a visible speaking style receives attention while careful organising is overlooked.","The issue is which actions are treated as evidence of leadership.","It challenges a narrow account without claiming that one personality type always leads better."]},"advanced-native-2082-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The photograph alone does not establish the lens through which people view leadership in that review; the recorded criteria concern organising and disagreement."],"options":["The photograph alone does not establish the lens through which people view leadership in that review; the recorded criteria concern organising and disagreement.","The notes identify speaking confidence as the only assessed quality.","The account gives no information about the criteria and describes only a photograph."]},"advanced-native-2082-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Everyone must use exactly the same criteria and reach the same judgement."],"options":["The discussion concerns assumptions or criteria used to interpret leadership.","Everyone must use exactly the same criteria and reach the same judgement.","The account can identify what a particular frame highlights or overlooks."]},"advanced-native-2082-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We should examine the lens through which people view leadership and include the missing decisions, not replace one personality stereotype with another."],"options":["We should examine the lens through which people view leadership and include the missing decisions, not replace one personality stereotype with another.","I would use quietness alone as the new test, without asking what decisions anyone made.","I thought leadership in this article meant public speaking rather than organising decisions, so I did not consider those decisions part of the evidence."]},"advanced-native-2082-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Our exhibition explores the lens through which people view leadership, and we invite a story about one concrete act of organising, care or resolving a disagreement. Please explain why it mattered, sharing only details you are comfortable and authorised to make public.","To explore the lens through which people view leadership, we would like to hear about a decision that helped people work together, whether or not it involved a public speech. You can choose an everyday example and tell us what made it useful, without naming anyone who has not agreed."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2083', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2083-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["It offered two proposal formats with shared criteria, while clarity still needed checking."],"options":["It had already confirmed that all applicants understood the instructions before offering the formats.","It accepted only written proposals and gave the criteria to existing members alone.","It offered two proposal formats with shared criteria, while clarity still needed checking.","It used separate role criteria for spoken proposals simply because they were not written."]},"advanced-native-2083-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Applicants could speak or write while being considered against shared requirements.","The proposal method could vary without giving one group a different role standard.","The club made the criteria available to everyone and kept a check on whether the instructions were understandable.","It tried to match opportunity with fairness through two formats and the same stated role criteria."],"options":["Applicants could speak or write while being considered against shared requirements.","The proposal method could vary without giving one group a different role standard.","The club made the criteria available to everyone and kept a check on whether the instructions were understandable.","It tried to match opportunity with fairness through two formats and the same stated role criteria."]},"advanced-native-2083-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A public invitation alone does not match opportunity with fairness when relevant preparation information reaches the groups at different times."],"options":["The timing difference concerns only an optional souvenir notice, not the criteria used in selection.","A public invitation alone does not match opportunity with fairness when relevant preparation information reaches the groups at different times.","The account gives all invited people the same preparation information at the same time."]},"advanced-n