very role he holds.","Context can clarify what the withdrawal looked like.","He disengaged from that discussion."]},"advanced-native-2108-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["I would not say she has checked out altogether when she is still contributing and answering decisions; absence and disengagement are different."],"options":["I would not say she has checked out altogether when she is still contributing and answering decisions; absence and disengagement are different.","I would use attendance in the room as the only measure of whether she is involved.","I assumed the submitted pages were old work because she was not present to discuss them in person."]},"advanced-native-2108-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I have checked out altogether from the editing work and need to be honest that I cannot promise new pages. I am stepping down, and I can return the existing files by Thursday so you can arrange the next stage without relying on me.","I have checked out altogether, but my vague promises have left you expecting more work from me. I am sorry; I will leave the role and hand back the current files on Thursday, rather than accept another assignment I will not complete."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2109', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2109-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The votes were equal, and neither date was announced as the winner."],"options":["Friday received more votes than Saturday.","The chair used an extra vote to settle the date.","Only five members expressed a preference.","The votes were equal, and neither date was announced as the winner."]},"advanced-native-2109-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The vote was tied rather than giving either date a majority.","Five members preferred one date and the other five preferred the alternative.","They were split down the middle, with five votes for each date.","Friday and Saturday each received half of the ten votes."],"options":["The vote was tied rather than giving either date a majority.","Five members preferred one date and the other five preferred the alternative.","They were split down the middle, with five votes for each date.","Friday and Saturday each received half of the ten votes."]},"advanced-native-2109-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The group has two preferences, but seven to three is not split down the middle in the numerical sense."],"options":["The account says the preferences were not counted.","The group has two preferences, but seven to three is not split down the middle in the numerical sense.","The presence of two options establishes five votes for each."]},"advanced-native-2109-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["A particular side has won under a stated tie-breaking rule."],"options":["A particular side has won under a stated tie-breaking rule.","More context can explain what happens after the tie.","The two sides were evenly divided."]},"advanced-native-2109-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The vote is split down the middle, so I can report the tie, but we need the agreed next step before declaring a date."],"options":["I thought getting half the votes was enough for Friday to win, even though Saturday received the other half.","I assumed t